  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Copper Creek is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want a kitchen and more space than a Wilderness Lodge hotel room, without leaving the boat to Magic Kingdom.</strong> The villas share the lodge's lobby, restaurants and dock.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups who can use a two-bedroom villa or a cabin.</strong> Both sleep eight. Cabins sit on Bay Lake and are priced in a different range than the villas in the lodge.</li>
      <li><strong>People who already like Wilderness Lodge and want to stay on the same grounds.</strong> This is not a separate hotel on the other side of property.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a studio or a one-bedroom.</strong> Official 2026 listings cap both at four adults. Boulder Ridge studios, by comparison, are listed as sleeping five.</li>
      <li><strong>A monorail from the building is the main reason you want a Magic Kingdom-area resort.</strong> This is a boat ride, plus a walk from some rooms to the dock.</li>
      <li><strong>You wanted a cabin but are comparing it with a two-bedroom villa on price alone.</strong> In 2026 a two-bedroom cabin ran about $2,823 to $5,440 a night at full price, tax included, which is well above the two-bedroom villa range of about $1,444 to $2,829.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

